# C# conventions (game scripts)

See also **engineering-standards** (always apply): remove replaced code, prefer helpers, high cohesion / loose coupling.

## Namespaces (match folder role)

- `GlobalDomination.GameData` — model types under `Core/GameData/`; **no** `UnityEngine.UI` / view references here.
- `GlobalDomination.Managers` — flow coordinators.
- `GlobalDomination` — cross-cutting helpers (e.g. `DiceRoller` in `Core/Helpers/`).
- `GlobalDomination.UI` — views and HUD; may depend on `GameData` / managers, not the reverse.

## Structure and coupling

- **Managers orchestrate;** widgets display and forward intent. Avoid **FindObjectOfType** / singleton sprawl for every little call—reuse existing access patterns in the file you edit.
- **Pure logic** (dice, table lookup, formatting rules) belongs in **`Core/Helpers/`** or `GameData` static tables, not buried in coroutines unless it is genuinely presentation sequencing.

## Large behaviours — partial classes

- Split by feature: `ClassName.Feature.partial.cs` or `ClassName.Feature.cs` (e.g. `UITestManager.StartupReveal.partial.cs`, `CityIconUI.BuildCityRollFlow.cs`).
- One **primary** file holds serialized fields and the class declaration; other parts are `public partial class` only—no duplicate field declarations.

## Unity patterns

- Inspector: `[SerializeField] private` and `[Header]`; **`FormerlySerializedAs`** when renaming serialized fields.
- **Singletons** (e.g. `GameManager.Instance`): keep established **Awake** duplicate-destroy behavior.

## Game data entry points

- Buildings / rolls: `BuildingRollTable.cs`
- Geography / countries: `CountryDatabase.cs`, `GameEnums.cs`
